From: Dustin Kirkland <dustin.kirkland@chainguard.dev>
Subject: pdftopdf: keep annotations without an appearance from aborting the job

Backport of upstream d3043e3 (OpenPrinting/libcupsfilters#246), source
change only (the upstream test plumbing does not apply to 2.2.1).

Flattening a link or form field with no /N appearance registered a Form
XObject under a heap-allocated name and then freed that name; PDFio keeps
the key pointer, so the page /XObject dictionary was corrupt when the
flattened file was written and cfFilterPDFToPDF() exited 1. Chrome's
direct-to-CUPS PDF hits this for every hyperlink.
